    <div class="caption-body" style="font-size:36px">The juice cup was not the reason.<br><br>By the time a big release happens, a sensitive child has often been holding a lot together for hours. The morning rush, the loud classroom, the effort of staying regulated all day. It builds quietly, and then one small thing becomes the tipping point.<br><br>This is not your child being difficult, and it is not you missing something. It is a nervous system that finally reached capacity.<br><br>When we look at the whole day instead of the final moment, the meltdown starts to make sense.</div>
